{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2245","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2245","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2245\",\"parent_revision\":\"a3d61b6eb42ef1a1e9891d7d85d8230afd3e20a6a3111a35244aed64ef6d3ecf\",\"root_revision\":\"a3d61b6eb42ef1a1e9891d7d85d8230afd3e20a6a3111a35244aed64ef6d3ecf\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: setup_gh.py does not auto-detect git remote \u2014 owner/repo is hardcoded across SKILL.md and CLAUDE.md examples\\nDate: 2026-05-22\\nGoal: Add owner/repo auto-detection to setup_gh.py and eliminate hardcoded literals from SKILL.md and CLAUDE.md\\n\\n**DECISION: APPROVED**\\n\\nAll 3 previously-MISSING conditions resolved via human confirmation (2026-05-22):\\n\\n**1. Owner/repo detection source \u2014 CONFIRMED**\\nUse the existing convention from `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py`:\\n- 4-pattern regex chain: `_SSH_REMOTE_RE`, `_HTTPS_REMOTE_RE`, `_SSH_PROTO_REMOTE_RE`, `_PROXY_REMOTE_RE`\\n- `_PROXY_REMOTE_RE = re.compile(r\\\".*/git/([^/]+/[^/]+?)(?:\\\\.git)?/?$\\\")` handles the 127.0.0.1 proxy\\n- Resolution order: `GITHUB_REPO` env var first, then git remote URL parsing via subprocess\\n- setup_gh.py is standalone \u2014 replicates the same regex patterns via subprocess (no import path to backlog_core)\\n\\n**2. Config write target \u2014 CONFIRMED**\\n`.dh/config.yaml` under `gh.repo` key. File already exists.\\n\\n**3. Documentation strategy \u2014 CONFIRMED**\\nTemplate-based approach:\\n- Checked-in template file (e.g., `gh-examples.md.template`) with `<owner/repo>` tokens\\n- `setup_gh.py` renders template \u2192 writes populated `gh-examples.md` (generated file)\\n- `CLAUDE.md` `<gh_cli_usage>` block: remove inline hardcoded examples, instruct agent to read the generated file\\n\\n**Derivable assumptions confirmed:**\\n- All 27 occurrences in SKILL.md are in command-example contexts (verified by grep)\\n- `<owner/repo>` placeholder token is consistent with existing CLAUDE.md convention\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nDrift between the literal string in SKILL.md/CLAUDE.md and the actual configured remote is undetectable. Agents copy the literal verbatim into commands targeting other repositories, hitting the wrong repo. There is no machine-readable record of the canonical owner/repo for the current checkout, forcing every agent that issues `gh` commands to either substitute manually or risk error.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **setup_gh.py does not auto-detect git remote \u2014 owner/repo is hardcoded across skill.md and claude.md examples** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/gh-skill.md \u2014 pattern: Proxy detection (Integration Opportunities)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-21)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n5/10 \u2014 Correctness risk: agents copy the hardcoded `-R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills` literal from SKILL.md/CLAUDE.md into commands targeting other repositories, hitting the wrong repo silently. Fix eliminates a category of silent mis-routing errors with zero behavior change for the current repo.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Agents in any repo other than `Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills` that follow the SKILL.md examples will issue `gh` commands against the wrong repository.\\n- Bottleneck: 27 occurrences of the hardcoded literal in `.claude/skills/gh/SKILL.md` and additional occurrences in `.claude/CLAUDE.md` must all be updated manually when the repo is forked or the remote changes. There is no machine-readable record of the canonical owner/repo for the current checkout.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Agents always use the correct owner/repo for the current checkout without manual substitution.\\n- SKILL.md and CLAUDE.md examples can use a placeholder token (e.g., `<owner/repo>`) or a computed value, eliminating the hardcoded literal.\\n- Forking or cloning the repository to a different remote requires no documentation updates.\\n- The proxy constraint (`127.0.0.1`) is documented once in setup_gh.py output, not buried in agent-facing documentation that may drift.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter running setup_gh.py, there is a machine-readable record of the canonical `owner/repo` for the current checkout \u2014 either written to a config file, an environment variable, or surfaced via a helper command \u2014 so agents can construct `-R <owner/repo>` dynamically rather than embedding a hardcoded literal. The proxy constraint (git remote points to 127.0.0.1) is handled by extracting the owner/repo from git remote metadata rather than the remote URL.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nObservable end state (one or more of):\\n- `setup_gh.py` detects `owner/repo` from git remote metadata (e.g., `git remote get-url origin` parsed for path components) and writes it to a config file (e.g., `.dh/config.yaml` or `.env`) or a project-local env var.\\n- `.claude/skills/gh/SKILL.md` examples reference the detected value rather than the hardcoded literal `Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills`.\\n- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` `<gh_cli_usage>` block references the detected value rather than the hardcoded literal.\\n- `grep -r \\\"Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills\\\" .claude/skills/gh/ .claude/CLAUDE.md` returns 0 matches (or only in a clearly-marked \\\"example output\\\" context).\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `setup_gh.py` reads git remote metadata and outputs the detected `owner/repo` to stdout or a config file without requiring manual input.\\n2. The detected `owner/repo` is accessible to agents without parsing git remote URLs directly.\\n3. `.claude/skills/gh/SKILL.md` no longer contains 27+ occurrences of the hardcoded literal `Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills` in agent-facing command examples (placeholder token or dynamic reference used instead).\\n4. `.claude/CLAUDE.md` `<gh_cli_usage>` block uses a placeholder or dynamic reference instead of the hardcoded literal.\\n5. An agent following SKILL.md examples in a repo with remote `owner2/repo2` will construct `gh ... -R owner2/repo2`, not `gh ... -R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills`.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Where should setup_gh.py write the detected owner/repo? Options: (a) `.dh/config.yaml` under a `gh.repo` key, (b) a dedicated `.dh/gh-config.json` file, (c) stdout only (caller captures and writes), (d) an environment variable set in the current shell session.\\n- The CLAUDE.md `<gh_cli_usage>` block is project-instruction context, not a plugin runtime file. Should examples use a literal placeholder like `<owner/repo>` that agents substitute at runtime, or should setup_gh.py populate CLAUDE.md directly?\\n- The git remote URL at `127.0.0.1` does not encode the real owner/repo. What is the authoritative source for owner/repo in this proxy configuration? (Candidates: `GITHUB_REPOSITORY` env var, a manually-set config value, or the GitHub API given `GITHUB_TOKEN`.)\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | .claude/skills/gh/scripts/setup_gh.py (770 lines, no remote detection) |\\n| Prior work | .claude/skills/gh/SKILL.md (27 hardcoded occurrences) |\\n| Prior work | .claude/CLAUDE.md gh_cli_usage block |\\n| Prior work | research/developer-tools/gh-skill.md (Integration Opportunities, line 238) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: Human input on owner/repo detection source (see Questions for Human)\\n- Blocks: None\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- The git remote at `127.0.0.1` does not contain the real owner/repo in the URL, so standard remote URL parsing will fail. The owner/repo detection strategy must account for the proxy configuration. Candidate sources: `GITHUB_REPOSITORY` env var (set in CI), GitHub API introspection via `GITHUB_TOKEN`, or a manually-configured `.dh/config.yaml` value. Implementation cannot proceed until the detection source is confirmed (see Questions for Human).\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall-Medium \u2014 setup_gh.py addition is small (detect + write config). The larger effort is updating 27+ occurrences in SKILL.md and the CLAUDE.md block to use placeholders or a dynamic reference. Effort is gated on human input about the proxy detection strategy.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:f7a5b787c73fd764dbbe835a69cf21e7 -->\\n\\n## Observed Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`./.claude/skills/gh/scripts/setup_gh.py` (770 lines) installs the gh binary but never inspects git remote configuration. A grep on 2026-05-10 for `remote`, `proxy`, `127.0.0.1`, or `git config` against the script returns zero matches.\\n\\nBecause the script does not detect the canonical owner/repo, every consumer must hardcode it:\\n- `./.claude/skills/gh/SKILL.md` contains the literal string `Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills` 30+ times across lines 76, 93, 96, 99, 102, 105, 112, 115, 118, 124, and beyond \u2014 verified via grep on 2026-05-10\\n- `./.claude/CLAUDE.md` `<gh_cli_usage>` block repeats the same hardcoded `-R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills` examples\\n- The repository operates behind a `127.0.0.1` git proxy (per CLAUDE.md `<gh_cli_usage>`), so `gh` cannot auto-discover the repo from the remote \u2014 the `-R` flag is mandatory on every invocation\\n</div>\\n\\n## Where Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `./.claude/skills/gh/scripts/setup_gh.py` \u2014 install script never reads git config\\n- `./.claude/skills/gh/SKILL.md` lines 73-79, 93, 96, 99, 102, 105, 112, 115, 118, 124+ \u2014 hardcoded repo literal\\n- `./.claude/CLAUDE.md` lines 446-470 \u2014 hardcoded repo literal in agent-facing instructions\\n</div>\\n\\n## User Provided Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry `./research/developer-tools/gh-skill.md` Integration Opportunities section line 238 suggests: \\\"Enhance setup_gh.py to detect and document proxy configuration so agents don't need to manually pass `-R` flags\\\". This is preserved as context, not a requirement \u2014 the implementation approach is for grooming/planning to determine.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry: ./research/developer-tools/gh-skill.md \u2014 pattern: Proxy detection / Integration Opportunities\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f4f7a3faeb7a23d84a3096f6e7f94626e9da58bdf8e39a2e12507ee497982ec9\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCQysw\"}"}